Advantages and Disadvantages of this, hence what came next
==========================================================

Advantages
----------
1. Protects Root Bridge election.
2. Prevents rogue switch attacks.
3. Prevents STP manipulation.
4. Reduces loop risks.
5. Improves network stability.
6. Reduces outage possibilities.
7. Strengthens Layer 2 security posture.

Disadvantages
-------------
1. Requires proper STP design.
2. More configuration overhead.
3. Incorrect placement may block valid links.
4. Troubleshooting can become more complex.
5. Does not detect physical one-way links automatically.

Hence what came next
--------------------
Loop Guard helps when BPDUs disappear unexpectedly.

However, it does not actively test whether the physical link is working in both directions.

Administrators wanted a mechanism that could detect one-way communication failures.

This led to:

UDLD (Unidirectional Link Detection)

which actively checks both sides of a fiber or Ethernet link and disables the link if a unidirectional condition is detected.

One-Shot Configuration
======================

Enable PortFast and BPDU Guard

Switch(config)# spanning-tree portfast default
Switch(config)# spanning-tree portfast bpduguard default


Protect Root Bridge

Switch(config)# interface g0/1
Switch(config-if)# spanning-tree guard root


Protect Against Missing BPDUs

Switch(config)# spanning-tree loopguard default


(Optional)
Configure Root Bridge

Switch(config)# spanning-tree vlan 10 root primary

Verification
============

show spanning-tree

show spanning-tree summary

show spanning-tree inconsistentports

show spanning-tree root

